WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.180
BETH: The world can seem a really
unpredictable and confusing place to

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.970
Individuals with autism, and they can
find any kind of change difficult.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.190
They often develop routines and
rituals as strategies they can use,

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:16.700
to cope with confusing sounds and
sights, events, people and places.

00:00:17.299 --> 00:00:20.910
JOE: They often prefer to have a daily
routine so that they know what is going

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.659
to happen every day, travelling the same
way to and from school or work, or eating

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.470
exactly the same food for breakfast.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.430
BETH: Some individuals may find
minor changes upsetting like the

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:35.119
positioning of simple things around
the house or introducing something new.

00:00:35.529 --> 00:00:39.930
Others find big events which create
major changes and upheaval distressing,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.880
like going on holiday, starting a
new school or moving to a new house.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.970
JOE: Some autistic people manage their
behaviour by using daily timetables to

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.579
help them see the structure of their day.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.820
They often have a need for structured
routine around daily activities such as

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.030
meals or bedtime and routines can become
almost ritualistic in nature, followed

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.620
precisely with great attention to detail.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:08.419
BETH: Some have rigid preferences
about things like food, such as always

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.219
wanting the same cereal or even only
eating food of a certain colour.

00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:15.550
Some may only wear clothes
made from specific fabrics

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.250
or again of a certain colour.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.869
JOE: Others find the need for
routine and sameness can go so

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.690
far, that it becomes an obsession.

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:28.600
People's dependence on routines can
increase during times of change, stress

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.729
or illness and may even become more
dominant or elaborate at these times.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.050
BETH: Individuals with Autism can
find changes to their routines

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:39.970
difficult, but they can be prepared
for change and supported through it.

